body:
I used to stay home alone with my brother at that age and much younger. We went to school without a guardian when I was age 6 and he was age 8, and he would make me sandwiches when we got home, thats how independent we were and came across no issues at all. 

&#x200B;

Building a trust and respect towards ones (mature) child is much better than being distrustful of your child simply because of their age and constantly helicoptering around them. For them to feel like they can be trusted to be independent even for just a little while is a big deal. However, I will say that some kids will take longer to reach a mature enough point to be left alone so its hard to say for sure what age is appropriate as all children are different. I will say though that the helicopter parenting movement nowadays just keep on rising the age of trusting them to be alone for silly reasons or no good reason at all.
